{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"16907fe07c4bb266d28d66d5996b9f9dfe9a0d925dbb68ba0e09c89b36b5cb0d","digest":{"component_or_area":"tests/interfaces/conftest.py - rebar repo template fixture","key_entities":["_rebar_repo_template","tests/interfaces/conftest.py","rebar.list_tickets()","rebar.init_repo()","REBAR_ROOT","pytest.MonkeyPatch.context()","tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin",".rebar"],"problem_keywords":["fixture assertion","template validation","test isolation","ticket store initialization"],"propositions":["The template fixture must assert no tickets exist inside the MonkeyPatch context where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned, not only in a separate test.","Without a fixture-level assertion, narrowed test runs (e.g., pytest tests/interfaces/store) lack protection against pre-seeded templates that would invert session-log count assertions.","The existing .rebar absence check and the new tickets assertion must both be retained and located appropriately (inside vs. outside the MonkeyPatch context) based on their environment requirements.","Pre-warming the template with tickets as an optimization would silently break invariant checks in queries and lifecycle tests that depend on template emptiness."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787320463781404001,"uuid":"4c049a12-228c-4321-a10f-8e94be83e3d7"}